    <h1>UNIT: SEMESTER 2 REVIEW<br>Lesson: Grammar Review - Technology Integration (AI Magic Board)</h1>

    <h2>I. OBJECTIVES</h2>
    <p>By the end of the lesson, Ss will be able to:</p>
    
    <p class="bold">1.1. Language knowledge and skills</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Consolidate and correctly apply 4 key grammatical themes of Semester 2:
            <ul>
                <li><b>Reported Speech:</b> Shifting tenses, changing pronouns, and updating time/place expressions.</li>
                <li><b>Past Continuous vs Past Simple:</b> Using <i>When</i> and <i>While</i>.</li>
                <li><b>Comparisons:</b> Transforming comparative forms into <i>not as... as</i> structures.</li>
                <li><b>Distance:</b> Using <i>What is the distance...</i> and <i>How far is it...</i>.</li>
            </ul>
        </li>
        <li>Improve writing accuracy through real-time sentence transformation exercises.</li>
    </ul>

    <p class="bold">1.2. Competences</p>
    <ul>
        <li><b>Critical Thinking:</b> Analyze sentence structures to apply complex grammar rules correctly.</li>
        <li><b>Digital Literacy:</b> Interact confidently with AI-based educational tools.</li>
        <li><b>Collaboration & Problem Solving:</b> Work in pairs/groups to brainstorm answers.</li>
    </ul>

    <p class="bold">1.3. Attributes</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Foster engagement and active participation via gamified learning (<b>AI Magic Board</b>).</li>
        <li>Promote a growth mindset through constructive AI feedback.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>II. TEACHING AIDS AND LEARNING MATERIALS</h2>
    <p><b>1. Teacher’s aids:</b> Projector / Interactive Whiteboard, Laptop with internet connection, <b>AI Magic Board Application</b> (Custom-built platform featuring digital slides, gamification, and AI automated assessment).</p>
    <p><b>2. Students’ aids:</b> Student’s workbook, notebook, pens, mini-whiteboards (optional).</p>

    <h2>III. ASSESSMENT EVIDENCE</h2>
    <table>
        <tr>
            <th>Performance Tasks</th>
            <th>Performance Products</th>
            <th>Assessment Tools</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>Participate in guided theory revision using interactive slides.</td>
            <td>Verbal responses & active engagement.</td>
            <td>T’s observation.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>Rewrite sentences based on 4 grammar modules on the AI Board.</td>
            <td>Written answers typed directly into the AI Magic Board.</td>
            <td><b>AI Automated Assessment</b> (Instant correct/incorrect feedback).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>Discussing why the AI accepted or rejected a submission.</td>
            <td>Arguments/Explanations in class.</td>
            <td>T’s feedback / Peers’ feedback.</td>
        </tr>
    </table>

    <h2>IV. PROCEDURES</h2>
    
    <p class="bold">A. Warm-up (5’)</p>
    <p>a) <b>Objective:</b> Introduce the AI learning tool and create a highly engaging atmosphere.</p>
    <p>b) <b>Content:</b> Exploring the "Main Menu" of the AI Magic Board.</p>
    <p>c) <b>Expected outcomes:</b> Students understand the lesson scope (4 Modules) and are excited.</p>
    <p>d) <b>Organization of the activity:</b></p>
    <table>
        <tr>
            <th style="width: 50%;">TEACHER’S ACTIVITIES</th>
            <th style="width: 50%;">STUDENTS’ ACTIVITIES</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>
                - Open the <b>AI Magic Board</b> application via projector.<br>
                - Introduce the concept: <i>"Today, your work will be judged by an AI Boss! We have 4 challenges to conquer."</i><br>
                - Show the visually appealing Main Menu and let students choose which module to tackle first.
            </td>
            <td>
                - Look at the smart board and observe the 4 modules.<br>
                - Vote on the module they want to review first (e.g., Reported Speech or When/While).
            </td>
        </tr>
    </table>

    <p class="bold">B. New Lesson: Grammar Revision (15’)</p>
    <p>a) <b>Objective:</b> Recall and reinforce the grammatical structures before testing.</p>
    <p>b) <b>Content:</b> Navigating through the interactive slides for the chosen module(s).</p>
    <p>c) <b>Expected outcomes:</b> Students grasp the formulas (e.g., 3 Golden Rules of Reported Speech).</p>
    <p>d) <b>Organization of the activity:</b></p>
    <table>
        <tr>
            <th style="width: 50%;">TEACHER’S ACTIVITIES</th>
            <th style="width: 50%;">STUDENTS’ ACTIVITIES</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>
                - Use the keyboard to navigate through the interactive theory slides.<br>
                - Explain key sections (e.g., The differences between <i>When</i> and <i>While</i>).<br>
                - Elicit answers for the "Quick-test" slide formats.
            </td>
            <td>
                - Take notes of the important formulas in their notebooks.<br>
                - Call out answers during the quick-test slides.<br>
                - Ask clarifying questions if any rule is forgotten.
            </td>
        </tr>
    </table>

    <p class="bold">C. Practice: The AI Challenge (20’)</p>
    <p>a) <b>Objective:</b> Apply theoretical knowledge into sentence transformation exercises.</p>
    <p>b) <b>Content:</b> Using the AI board to type and check rewritten sentences.</p>
    <p>c) <b>Expected outcomes:</b> Students successfully rewrite sentences; learn immediately from AI hints.</p>
    <p>d) <b>Organization of the activity:</b></p>
    <table>
        <tr>
            <th style="width: 50%;">TEACHER’S ACTIVITIES</th>
            <th style="width: 50%;">STUDENTS’ ACTIVITIES</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>
                - Click "CHALLENGE ACCEPTED!" to enter the AI Board.<br>
                - Provide a sentence from the Question Bank.<br>
                - Type the student's answer into the giant input box and click <b>"AI CHECK"</b>.<br>
                - <b>If Correct:</b> Celebrate together with the screen's Confetti effect.<br>
                - <b>If Incorrect:</b> Use the AI's feedback and the screen shake effect to discuss why it was wrong. Invite another student to correct it.
            </td>
            <td>
                - Work individually or in pairs to rewrite the sentences on paper or mini-whiteboards.<br>
                - Volunteer to stand up and dictate the answer to the Teacher.<br>
                - Analyze the AI's feedback if the answer is rejected.<br>
                - Re-attempt structural corrections.
            </td>
        </tr>
    </table>

    <p class="bold">D. Consolidation & Homework (5’)</p>
    <p>a) <b>Objective:</b> Summarize the lesson and assign self-study tasks.</p>
    <p>b) <b>Content:</b> Wrap up the 4 modules and assign workbook exercises.</p>
    <p>c) <b>Expected outcomes:</b> Students remember the core takeaway from the AI interaction.</p>
    <p>d) <b>Organization of the activity:</b></p>
    <table>
        <tr>
            <th style="width: 50%;">TEACHER’S ACTIVITIES</th>
            <th style="width: 50%;">STUDENTS’ ACTIVITIES</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>
                - Summarize which grammatical points were the hardest to get past the AI.<br>
                - Assign homework: Complete the remaining sentences from the Semester 2 revision outline on paper.
            </td>
            <td>
                - Note down the homework assignment.<br>
                - Share their favorite part of the AI Magic Board experience.
            </td>
        </tr>
    </table>

</body>
</html>
